        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Of course, we very much want to build mil-tech cooperation between Ukraine and Japan. G2G, but also B2B, as now more than 70% of the defense industry in Ukraine is in the private sector. I think we can increase our trade turnover, especially if we focus on the defense-industrial base. \n\nI do know there are differences between our legal systems. But in my view, when we speak about defense, there are no neutral nations. Sometimes, you don’t even have a big army, but you need a big defense sector, because it is about sea monitoring, intelligence and demining drones, and, of course, air defense and cybersecurity, as well as food security.\n\nI think that we can be useful to each other. We wanted to have a Drone Deal with Japan. Perhaps you will need some defensive equipment. This is, of course, up to Japan to decide. Again, we are thankful for all the support.\n\nFrom an interview with NHK. (1/3)"
        },
